        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 61 (width for one central pineapple column with open mesh on each side)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1 (base mesh)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tr into the 8th ch from hook. *Ch 2, skip 2 ch, tr into the next ch*. Repeat across. Turn. (19 mesh squares.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Starting the pineapple (rows 2 to 14)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2: Ch 5. *Tr into the next tr, ch 2*. Repeat to the 9th tr (centre). Into the 9th tr: ch 3, [tr, ch 1] x 13, tr, ch 3. Continue in mesh to end. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rows 3 to 13: Work mesh on the outer squares. For the pineapple centre: on each right-side row work dc into each ch-1 arc of the pineapple. On each wrong-side row work ch-5 arcs over the dc stitches, decreasing by one arc each time (12 arcs on row 3, 11 on row 5, and so on down to 1 arc on row 13)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 14: Ch 5. Dc into the one remaining arc. Ch 5. Continue in mesh. This closes the pineapple point."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Begin the next pineapple at Row 2 immediately. Repeat until the scarf reaches 170 cm. Fasten off. Wet block carefully to open up each motif."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
